273
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,360
I was pretty sure I wanted you...

274
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,820
...but I just thought we should meet face to face.

275
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:58,600
I've made my decision.

276
00:12:00,340 --> 00:12:01,080
I choose them.

277
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:04,100
Oh, my God, this is great.

278
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,480
This is so great. Did you hear that?

279
00:12:06,580 --> 00:12:07,720
Yeah, I did.

280
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,210
Hey.

281
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:12,340
Thank you. Thank you so much.

282
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:16,820
You are so going to heaven!

283
00:12:23,594 --> 00:12:25,932
We got some really great stuff.

284
00:12:25,952 --> 00:12:27,111
Yeah.

285
00:12:27,131 --> 00:12:29,821
Yeah, but I'm not sure about some of the bras I got.

286
00:12:30,162 --> 00:12:32,081
Really? Do you want to try some of them on for me?

287
00:12:32,101 --> 00:12:33,371
Okay.

288
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:35,800
Wait, are we in Joey's imagination?

289
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:42,000
Oh, no. I took one of Ross' bags by mistake.

290
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:43,720
And one of mine is missing.

291
00:12:44,710 --> 00:12:45,580
Ross probably has it.

292
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,720
You'll get it from him later.

293
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:54,880
So, what do you think?

294
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:00,240
I think we're not wearing the same shirt anymore.

295
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:04,780
Yeah. Yeah, Rachel picked it out for me.

296
00:13:04,900 --> 00:13:06,660
She told me to trust her, and you know what?

297
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:07,580
I'm glad I did.

298
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,740
I turned quite a few heads on my way over here.

299
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:14,820
Dude, I really don't think you should be wearing that.

300
00:13:16,211 --> 00:13:17,771
I see.

301
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,860
Somebody's afraid of a little competition with the ladies?

302
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:24,240
Looks like someone is the ladies!

303
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:29,080
You're just jealous because you couldn't pull this off.

304
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:32,260
Yeah. Now if you'll excuse me, I have a date.

305
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:38,140
See? All eyes on me!

306
00:13:44,140 --> 00:13:46,320
We are not signing those papers.

307
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:47,140
Why not?

308
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:49,920
It's wrong. They made a mistake.

309
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,280
They think we're somebody else.

310
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:53,540
God works in mysterious ways.

311
00:13:54,900 --> 00:13:56,020
You have got to stop.

312
00:13:57,460 --> 00:13:59,020
But she liked us.

313
00:13:59,040 --> 00:14:00,700
She likes Doctor Chandler

314
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:01,780
and Reverend Monica.

315
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:04,120
If you think about it,

316
00:14:04,340 --> 00:14:05,620
I'm kind of like a reverend.

317
00:14:06,350 --> 00:14:09,340
I mean, as a chef, I serve God

318
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:12,120
by feeding the hungry and poor.

319
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:15,300
Your veal chop is 34.95!

320
00:14:17,736 --> 00:14:18,666
Come on,

321
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:20,360
I just-- I think we've been given an opportunity.

322
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,260
The mistake's already made.

323
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:23,780
They're writing up the papers now.

324
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:25,420
But we're not the ones she chose.

325
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,980
How can you feel okay about this?

326
00:14:29,728 --> 00:14:31,118
Because.

327
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:34,680
We may not be who she thinks we are...

328
00:14:35,060 --> 00:14:37,860
...but no one will ever love that baby more than us.

329
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:39,760
- I know.  - I mean, who knows...

330
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,260
...how long it's gonna take for someone else

331
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:42,300
to give us a baby?

332
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:45,280
What if no one ever picks us?

333
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:46,560
Oh, honey....

334
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:48,200
Please?

335
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:50,880
Please. We are so close.

336
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:55,220
Monica, I want a baby too.

337
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:58,440
But this woman is giving away her child.

338
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:00,960
She deserves to know who it's going to.

339
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:09,980
Okay. You're right.

340
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:15,500
So we'll tell the truth.

341
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:16,520
And who knows, you know?

342
00:15:16,680 --> 00:15:18,260
Maybe she'll like us for us.

343
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:22,500
Maybe she will.

344
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:25,960
Why couldn't I have been a reverend?

345
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:27,100
You're Jewish.

346
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:31,180
Technicality!

347
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,360
Garden salad for the lady.

348
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:41,400
Oh, that looks great. Good ordering.

349
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:44,780
Seafood platter for the gentleman,

350
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:46,520
and extra fries.

351
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:47,500
Enjoy.

352
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:52,520
Those fries look delicious.

353
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:54,640
I didn't know you liked French fries.

354
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:57,300
Help yourself. What's mine is yours.

355
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,240
Wow, are those stuffed clams?

356
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:11,220
Yes, they are my stuffed clams.

357
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:16,360
How about those fries, though, huh?

358
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:19,880
- They are delicious.  - Yeah.

359
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:25,920
You are beautiful, you know that?

360
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:29,960
That is so sweet.

361
00:16:32,099 --> 00:16:33,729
Okay, then.

362
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:47,100
Now look what you did!

363
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:50,200
What? What is the matter with you?

364
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:51,060
I don't like it

365
00:16:51,060 --> 00:16:53,800
when people take food off of my plate, okay?

366
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:56,020
But you said, "What's mine is yours."

367
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:57,180
Well, I didn't mean it!

368
00:16:59,104 --> 00:17:01,064
Fine. Sorry,

369
00:17:01,150 --> 00:17:02,940
I didn't think it was that big a deal.

370
00:17:05,195 --> 00:17:07,015
No, I'm sorry. I....

371
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:09,240
I'm overreacting, okay?

372
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:11,340
It's just, when it comes to food, l...

373
00:17:11,820 --> 00:17:13,300
...have certain rules...

374
00:17:13,840 --> 00:17:14,960
...okay? I mean...

375
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:16,880
...there are things you do,

376
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:19,560
and, you know, things that you don't do.

377
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,260
Wow, this place looks great.

378
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:30,760
Oh, you are gonna love it.

379
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:33,800
And I'm so glad we're finally doing this.

380
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:35,540
- Me too.  - Here.

381
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,480
So this was fun.

382
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:58,540
I really am sorry about, you know, before.

383
00:17:58,560 --> 00:18:00,280
And I want to make sure you know

384
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:01,660
I really do like you.

385
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:04,360
Sure, just not as much as clams.

386
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:05,820
Well, stuffed clams....

387
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:10,060
Chocolate torte for the lady.

388
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,320
Cheesecake for the gentleman.

389
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:13,700
Excuse me, sir.

390
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:16,840
There seems to be some sort of red crap on my cheesecake.

391
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,040
Yes, that's a raspberry coulis.

392
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:23,200
I'm so stupid ordering cheesecake,

393
00:18:23,270 --> 00:18:24,000
trying to be healthy.

394
00:18:37,943 --> 00:18:39,853
Oh, no.

395
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:41,780
This is work. I should call in.

396
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:42,700
Can you excuse me?

397
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:44,060
Yeah, sure. No problem.

398
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:48,180
What are you doing?

399
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:50,560
I thought you don't share food?

400
00:18:50,860 --> 00:18:51,720
Sure I do.

401
00:18:52,617 --> 00:18:53,897
Coulis?

402
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:57,600
No. If I can't have your clams,

403
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:58,780
you can't have my dessert.

404
00:18:58,940 --> 00:19:00,300
This is a two-way street.

405
00:19:03,060 --> 00:19:03,660
Really?

406
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:06,460
Really.

407
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:09,120
Now this all better be here when I come back.

408
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:12,640
Yeah, of course. I can control myself.

409
00:19:26,180 --> 00:19:27,360
Stop staring at me!

410
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:40,860
Just a tiny little....

411
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:57,660
I'm not even sorry.

412
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:03,820
- Hi.  - Hey.

413
00:20:04,900 --> 00:20:08,580
So these are the preliminary forms for an open adoption.

414
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:10,020
There's a lot to go over,

415
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:11,800
but I'll explain as we go through.

416
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:16,260
- Is that a picture? - Yeah.

417
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:18,860
It's a sonogram they took of the baby last week.

418
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:21,700
I thought you might want to see it.

419
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,360
Look, doctor.

420
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:35,940
Look, before we sign anything,

421
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:37,700
we really have to talk.

422
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:43,100
We're not who you think we are.

423
00:20:43,260 --> 00:20:44,280
I don't understand.

424
00:20:44,540 --> 00:20:46,420
The agency must have made a mistake.

425
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:47,880
My wife is not a reverend,

426
00:20:47,890 --> 00:20:48,840
and I'm not a doctor.

427
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,320
- What? - That's impossible.

428
00:20:51,580 --> 00:20:53,540
I could perform an operation on you

429
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:54,600
and prove it if you'd like.

430
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:58,980
I have to check your file. Excuse me.

431
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:01,140
So who are you?

432
00:21:02,020 --> 00:21:04,880
Our names really are Monica and Chandler. We're from New York.

433
00:21:04,940 --> 00:21:07,280
Yeah, but the important thing to know about us...

434
00:21:08,020 --> 00:21:10,240
...is how much we would care for this little baby.

435
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,800
So you lied to me before?

436
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:16,080
Well, we "bore false witness."

437
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,820
See? I could be a reverend.

438
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,960
I can't believe this.

439
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:25,760
But we were hoping that since we told you the truth...

440
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:27,300
...that you still might consider--

441
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:28,540
Giving you my baby?

442
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:31,380
You think I'd give you my child after this?

443
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,680
You don't have to decide now.

444
00:21:32,820 --> 00:21:34,200
If you look at our file--

445
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:36,440
I don't want to look at your file. This is over.

446
00:21:42,140 --> 00:21:42,860
Erica, wait.

447
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:45,440
I have nothing to say to you.

448
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:47,920
Look, you have every reason to be upset.

449
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:49,660
We did lie.

450
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:51,320
But only because we've been waiting

451
00:21:51,380 --> 00:21:53,720
and trying to have a baby for so long.

452
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,880
And we don't know how long it's gonna be

453
00:21:55,880 --> 00:21:57,520
before we get another chance again.

454
00:21:57,620 --> 00:21:59,700
Why don't you ask the reverend to pray on it?

455
00:22:00,059 --> 00:22:02,909
Erica, please.

456
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:04,460
Just consider us.

457
00:22:05,300 --> 00:22:06,480
Ask them to see our file.

458
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:09,040
Our last name's Bing.

459
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:11,740
My wife's a chef, and I'm in advertising.

460
00:22:13,280 --> 00:22:14,440
Oh, yeah.

461
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:17,260
I actually liked you guys.

462
00:22:19,100 --> 00:22:20,260
But it doesn't matter.

463
00:22:20,260 --> 00:22:21,580
Because what you did was wrong.

464
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:23,760
But you did like us.

465
00:22:24,220 --> 00:22:25,280
And you should.

466
00:22:27,080 --> 00:22:28,560
My wife's an incredible woman.

467
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:32,400
She is loving, and devoted and caring.

468
00:22:33,940 --> 00:22:35,420
And don't tell her I said this,

469
00:22:35,540 --> 00:22:36,620
but the woman's always right.

470
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:43,880
I love my wife more than anything in this world.

471
00:22:46,118 --> 00:22:47,568
And it...

472
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:51,240
It kills me that I can't give her a baby.

473
00:22:57,860 --> 00:22:59,140
I really want a kid.

474
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:02,680
And when that day finally comes,

475
00:23:02,700 --> 00:23:04,060
I'll learn how to be a good dad.

476
00:23:05,580 --> 00:23:06,460
But my wife...

477
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:09,400
...she's already there.

478
00:23:10,300 --> 00:23:12,500
She's a mother...

479
00:23:13,620 --> 00:23:14,280
...without a baby.

480
00:23:22,808 --> 00:23:24,338
Please?

481
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,400
You still want that baby?

482
00:23:54,140 --> 00:23:55,800
God bless you, Chandler Bing!

483
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:12,060
Turns out this sweater is made for a woman.

484
00:24:15,180 --> 00:24:16,960
So why are you still wearing it?

485
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:18,080
Because it's soft.

486
00:24:20,620 --> 00:24:21,640
Hey, so how was your date?

487
00:24:22,660 --> 00:24:23,280
Not so good.

488
00:24:26,900 --> 00:24:29,460
Well, looks like it's just the two of us tonight,

489
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:29,980
huh, buddy?

490
00:24:31,020 --> 00:24:32,260
Yeah. And you know what?

491
00:24:32,540 --> 00:24:33,780
We could do a lot worse.

492
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:34,980
- Yeah. - Yeah.

493
00:24:38,820 --> 00:24:40,880
Joey doesn't share food!

